# Code owners -- a change to any path below REQUIRES the maintainer's review before it can merge.
# Pair this with branch protection on `main` that has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
# These are the supply-chain-critical surfaces for a Python package: the CI workflows, the
# dependency declaration that decides what gets installed, and the shipped data that decides
# what every note resolves to.
#
# The data directory joined this list when the sound palette started shipping. It carries
# identifiers rather than code, so a tampered entry cannot execute anything -- but it CAN
# silently change which sound every note plays, and no test can tell an intentional palette
# change from a malicious one.
#
# NOTE: @adiazpar is the maintainer's GitHub handle -- verify it matches the account that owns
# the repo (an invalid handle here is silently ignored by GitHub, i.e. no enforcement).

/.github/                    @adiazpar
/pyproject.toml              @adiazpar
/src/snapmap_midi/data/      @adiazpar
/tools/                      @adiazpar
